{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793020000000-engineer-8f1b.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-15 09:00:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-15 16:00:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: 8f-1 implementation per the Architect ruling (steps 0,1,2,3,4a,5), uncommitted\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-15 16:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: your earlier stop was correct; the Architect ruled; same author implements; Fable reviews before commit\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8f1k (branch srvm-phase8f1 @ d43afbe3, clean). Read ./collab/1792050511876-architect-8f1-ruling.report.md and EXECUTE its section 2 steps 0, 1, 2, 3, 4a and 5 EXACTLY, in order, running each step's lane before the next. NOT in this task: step 4b (ucf.cljc shrink, ucf_test deletion), deleting semantic.cljc/linearize.cljc/code.cljc and their tests, the demos, test_utils, the 38 requirer ports, the rename (all 8f-3/8f-2). Ten C4 files under test/yang/python/antlr remain editable (owner freeze); nothing else under test/yang or src/yang; no docs edits. Step 1 gate: the three pinned literals (descriptor-declares-the-contract 7b7c6ae9...f3489, the four golden-corpus pairs, golden-descriptor-hash-test aa757659...7e74c) must stay byte-unchanged in the test files; if they fail, STOP and report BLOCKED, do not touch the literals. If any step needs a decision the ruling does not give, STOP and report. No commit, no stage.\nVerification FOREGROUND sequential per the ruling (kondo no new warnings; per-step lanes; step 5: bb test:clj quick tier per docs/agents/build-n-test.md; the sandbox may deny the loopback head-board-test: say so; do not run Node/Dart, the orchestrator does). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-8f1b.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID: per-step results with counts, the pinned