{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'vector-operand-table' src/cljc/yin/vm/code.cljc; sed -n '293,354p' src/cljc/yin/vm/code.cljc; sed -n '610,685p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '215,270p' test/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc; sed -n '325,360p' test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj; rg -n 'handoff' test/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc; tail -20 collab/1792050511876-architect-8f1-ruling.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"218:(def vector-operand-table\n287:  (mapv second (get vector-operand-table (nth t 0))))\n318:            (when-not (= (inc (count (get vector-operand-table (nth t 0))))\n\n(defn- nonempty\n  \"Rule 1. An empty vector names pc 0, where the first instruction belongs;\n   so does anything a pc cannot index: the canonical form is a vector\n   (UCF §7.3.2), so a list outer is not the form at any length.\"\n  [v]\n  (when-not (and (vector? v) (pos? (count v)))\n    (tuple-defect :nonempty 0)))\n\n\n(defn- mnemonic\n  \"Rule 2.\"\n  [v]\n  (some (fn [pc]\n          (when-not (contains? mnemonics (mnemonic-of (nth v pc)))\n            (tuple-defect :mnemonic pc)))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- arity\n  \"Rule 3. §2.4's operand table as saturated and made positional by UCF\n   §7.3.2: the mnemonic plus exactly its operands.\"\n  [v]\n  (some (fn [pc]\n          (let [t (nth v pc)]\n            (when-not (= (inc (count (get vector-operand-table (nth t 0))))\n                         (count t))\n              (tuple-defect :arity pc))))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- operand-kind\n  \"Rule 4. An operand is judged only by the kind §7.5 gives it.\"\n  [v]\n  (some (fn [pc]\n          (let [t (nth v pc)\n                kinds (tuple-kinds t)]\n            (some (fn [i]\n                    (let [check (get operand-kind-checks (nth kinds (dec i)))]\n                      (when (and check (not (check (nth t i))))\n                        (tuple-defect :operand-kind pc))))\n                  (range 1 (count t)))))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- saturation\n  \"Rule 5. A saturated operand is materialized in a canonical tuple; a nil\n   one names its pc.\"\n  [v]\n  (some (fn [pc]\n          (let [t (nth v pc)]\n            (when (some #(and (contains? saturated-operands [(nth t 0) %])\n                              (nil? (nth t %)))\n                        (range 1 (count t)))\n              (tuple-defect :saturation pc))))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- target-bounds\n  \"Rule 6. A resolved pc must be an integer inside the segment.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [length (count v)]\n   `:exporting` or `:ended`, read from `:yin.k/gate`.\"\n  [state]\n  (:yin.k/gate state))\n\n\n;; Bytecode Opcodes\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Shared instruction set for stack and register bytecode VMs.\n\n(def opcode-table\n  {:literal 1,\n   :load-var 2,\n   :move 3,\n   :lambda 4,\n   :call 5,\n   :return 6,\n   :branch 7,\n   :jump 8,\n   :gensym 9,\n   :store-get 10,\n   :store-put 11,\n   :stream-make 12,\n   :stream-put 13,\n   :stream-cursor 14,\n   :stream-next 15,\n   :stream-close 16,\n   :park 17,\n   :resume 18,\n   :current-cont 19,\n   :tailcall 20,\n   :dao.stream.apply/call 21,\n   :push 22,\n   :halt 23,\n   :define 24})\n\n\n#?(:clj\n   (defmacro opcase\n     \"Dispatch on a numeric opcode using keyword mnemonics.\n      Resolved at compile-time to a standard 'case' over integers.\"\n     [op-expr & clauses]\n     (let [default (when (odd? (count clauses)) (last clauses))\n           paired (if default (butlast clauses) clauses)\n           pairs (partition 2 paired)\n           ;; Keep a local literal map so CLJD macro host compilation\n           ;; does not depend on resolving `opcode-table` as a host\n           ;; symbol.\n           opcodes {:literal 1,\n                    :load-var 2,\n                    :move 3,\n                    :lambda 4,\n                    :call 5,\n                    :return 6,\n                    :branch 7,\n                    :jump 8,\n                    :gensym 9,\n                    :store-get 10,\n                    :store-put 11,\n                    :stream-make 12,\n                    :stream-put 13,\n                    :stream-cursor 14,\n                    :stream-next 15,\n                    :stream-close 16,\n                    :park 17,\n                    :resume 18,\n                    :current-cont 19,\n                    :tailcall 20,\n                    :dao.stream.apply/call 21,\n                    :push 22,\n                    :halt 23,\n                    :define 24}\n           resolved (mapcat (fn [[kw body]] [(get opcodes kw) body]) pairs)]\n       `(case (int ~op-expr) ~@resolved ~@(when default [default])))))\n\n\n(def schema\n                'c {:type :stream/cursor, :source (u/v 's)}\n                (u/then\n                  {:type :stream/put, :target (u/v 's), :val put-value}\n                  (u/then\n                    garbage\n                    (u/let1 'x {:type :stream/next, :source (u/v 'c)}\n                            read-value)))))]\n    (run-all\n      (u/mark-tails ast)\n      (fn [final]\n        (is (vm/machine-data? (vm/value final)))\n        (is (= (canon-ints [(f/value \"2^64\") [42]])\n               (canon-ints (:items (vm/value final))))\n            (pr-str (select-keys final [:value :error :status])))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow pinning-test\n  (slow/guard \"pinning-test\" pinning))\n\n\n(defn- cell-refusal\n  []\n  (run-all\n    (guest '(py/list (py/vconj [] (py/int-lit \"10000000000000000\"))))\n    (fn [final]\n      (let [r (handoff/export-task final (fn [_h] nil))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status r)))\n        (is (= :cell (:yin.k/kind r))))))\n  (run-all\n    (guest '(yin/def (quote held) (py/dict-new)))\n    (fn [final]\n      (let [r (try (engine/lift-slice final :segment/own ['held])\n                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                     (ex-data e)))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status r)))\n        (is (= :cell (:yin.k/kind r))))))\n  (run-all\n    (guest '(yin/def (quote held)\n              (py/tuple (py/vconj [] (py/int-lit \"10000000000000000\")))))\n    (fn [final]\n      (let [r (engine/lift-slice final :segment/own ['held])]\n        (is (= {} (:cells r)))\n        (is (= (canon-ints [(f/value \"2^64\")])\n               (canon-ints\n                 (filter integer-host/big-carrier?\n                         (tree-seq coll? seq (get-in r [:slice 'held]))))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow cell-refusal-test\n  (slow/guard \"cell-refusal-test\" cell-refusal))\n   ;; the expander consumer's macro store\n   \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"\n   {[\"inject-last-value\" \"update\"] 1\n    [\"make-expander\" :map] 1}\n   ;; the content source descriptor: `:store` names a dao.jing byte-store\n   ;; handle the linker interpreter serves content from, never a VM store\n   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc\"\n   {[\"composition\" :map] 1}\n   ;; the handoff demo: shipped definitions, checked\n   \"src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc\"\n   {[\"datoms->semantic-vm\" \"update\"] 1}\n   ;; a JVM demo moving one VM's whole store to another\n   \"src/clj/yin/demo.clj\"\n   {[\"run-demo\" \"assoc\"] 1}\n   ;; the handoff lower's isolated-store install (UCF 7.6.2): every\n   ;; carried key goes through store-put -- a reserved key inside a\n   ;; tampered body refuses -- and the checked slice then lands on the\n   ;; fresh receiver in one write.  D10 renamed the lower to\n   ;; resume-task* and moved child restoration behind\n   ;; isolated-receiver, which pre-seeds the receiver's isolated store\n   ;; (grant-authorized state only, D10's inputs ruling)\n   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc\"\n   {[\"isolated-receiver\" \"assoc\"] 1\n    [\"resume-task*\" \"assoc\"] 1\n    [\"resume-task*\" \"engine/store-put\"] 1}\n   ;; display projections of a VM's store in the browser demos\n   \"src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs\"\n   {[\"walker-cesk\" :map] 1}\n   \"src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs\"\n   {[\"vm->cesk\" :map] 1}\n   ;; the expander's macro store: harvest refuses the reserved key,\n   ;; post-harvest installs only harvested names, make-ctx refuses a\n   ;; seeded store binding it, expand-batch threads the checked store\n   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"\n   {[\"harvest\" \"assoc\"] 1\n    [\"harvest\" \"dissoc\"] 1\n25:            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n240:      (let [r (handoff/export-task final (fn [_h] nil))]\n\n**Step 3 — R3.** `git rm src/cljc/yin/vm/completion.cljc test/yin/vm/completion_test.cljc`; `vm.cljc` (:612-680 `opcode-table`+`opcase`, :1839-1894 segment queries, docstring :1875); `scan_test`, `query_test`, `cell_test`, `linker/publish_test`, `debruijn_code_test` as listed in R3; `linker.cljc:2057` and `driver.clj:8` docstrings (R4). Lane: `dao.space.query-test`, `yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test`, `yin.vm.cell-test`, `yin.vm.linker.publish-test`, `yin.vm.debruijn-code-test`, `yin.vm.mint-test`. (`cell_test`/`publish_test`/`query_test` still require `yin.vm.semantic`/`linearize` elsewhere; they compile because those files still exist until 8f-3.)\n\n**Step 4 — R2 + R5.** `ucf.cljc` to `code-address`; `git rm test/yin/vm/ucf_test.cljc`; `rule_r_test` (one deftest); `vm.cljc:1796`, `scan.cljc:76`, `scan_test:254`, `query_test` footprint assertion. **`semantic.cljc:669` calls `ucf/batch->canonical-instruction-vector`**: in this step replace that call site's function with a 3-line private copy? No — rule: `semantic.cljc` is deleted in 8f-3, so step 4 would break it. Therefore step 4 is split: **4a** (R5 `:push` edits and the `rule_r_test` deftest removal) lands in 8f-1; **4b** (shrinking `ucf.cljc`, deleting `ucf_test.cljc`) moves to 8f-3 and is the first `git rm`/edit of that slice, in the same commit as `semantic.cljc`'s deletion. Lane for 4a: `yin.vm.rule-r-test`, `yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test`, `dao.space.query-test`.\n\n**Step 5 — gate for 8f-1.** `clj -M:kondo` (no new warnings; the deleted files' warnings vanish), `bb test:clj` quick tier, then Node and Dart lanes per `build-n-test.md` (clean `lib/cljd-out` first). Report with: the deleted-test ledger (handoff/checkpoint: 0 deftests, already gone in 8d; `completion_test` 19 deleted, table in R3 as the replacement column; `rule_r_test` 1 deleted; `scan_test` 1 deleted; `cell_test` 1 deleted; `query_test` 1 deleted; `publish_test` 0 deleted, 1 narrowed), the pinned literals before/after, deftest count before/after.\n\nCommit shape for 8f-1: one commit, `refactor(yin.vm): the stack grammar is debruijn-code's own data; old transport sources, dependency completion and the v3 footprint residue are out (8f-1)`. Architect sign-off before commit, as standing.\n\n## 3. What must wait\n\n- **8f-2** (plan Q3 commit 1): `git mv` `semantic_register*` → `semantic*`, tests likewise. Unchanged by this ruling.\n- **8f-3** (plan Q3 commit 2 plus the deletions): `git rm semantic.cljc linearize.cljc code.cljc`, `semantic_test` (25) `linearize_test` (23) `code_test` (13), **plus step 4b** (`ucf.cljc` shrink, `ucf_test` 24), the three demos, `test_utils.cljc` (`create-vm` is already the walker; `run-encoder-session:167` and the `linearize`/`semantic` requires go), the ~38 test requirers incl. the 9 C4 files, `ucf/remote_test`, the ports of `semantic_engine_test`/`semantic_ffi_test`/`semantic_stream_observer_test`, `linked_harness` is already ported (8c). Gate: the phase gate of plan row 8f.\n- **8g**: every doc line in R6.\n\n## 4. Invariants checked\n\nA is the only code identity: H stays a derived checksum (`image-hash` docstring already says so); R1 moves data, not identity. Tree always available: nothing here lowers from A alone; completion's tree-less segment scoping is what dies. Derive, don't persist: no new table, no v4 batch grammar, no safepoint port; the one new literal replaces a derivation whose source dies. Minimal diff: zero new namespaces; the only additions are a private set and one rewritten deftest. No backend widening: 23 mnemonics in, 23 out, `lowering-contract-version` stays 2. Codex implements, Fable reviews.\n\nRULING-READY\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
